<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112297" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρεν-όω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρήν</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make wise, instruct,
				inform,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				337
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				754
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				526
			</span></i> (troch.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρενώσω δ᾽ οὐκέτ᾽ ἐξ
				αἰνιγμάτων,</span> i.e. <i>will teach</i> plainly, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1183
			</span></i>; poet. Verb, used by <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.1.5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. τινὰ εἴς τι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.6.1
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Lib.</u>
				p.52
			</span></i> O.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεφρενωμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Lex.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρενωθῆναι οὐδὲ πρὸς αὐτῆς τῆς
					Ἀθηνᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					7.225b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be high-minded, elated,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>2 Ma.</u>
				11.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				101.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ.</span> is prob. a late spelling of
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρονῶν</span> (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρονέω</span> IV fin.) in the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῶν καὶ φρενῶν.</span></div>
